    "body": "@wangyicong52 — 🎉 DSpark is now enabled and serving inference in production-shaped config, and this fix is what unblocked it. Thank you!\n\nHowever, this validates the **static-K path only** — `num_speculative_tokens` is fixed at 5 for the entire run. Our ultimate goal is **dynamically scheduled drafted tokens** (dynamic speculative decoding) for DSpark, and that path is currently non-functional on the V2 model runner: `scheduler_output.num_spec_tokens_to_schedule` is never read (`vllm/v1/worker/gpu/model_runner.py` has zero references), so `num_speculative_tokens_per_batch_size` silently has no effect (#51510). Not a blocker for this PR — flagging it because the acceptance curve decays steeply (0.85 → 0.27 across the 5 positions), which is exactly the regime where a per-batch-size K would pay off.\n\n**Environment**\n- 4× H200 (SM90), TP=4, `DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash` (`DeepseekV41ForCausalLM`)\n- Base `vllm/vllm-openai:deepseekv41-flash-0909` (`0.1.dev20904+g179dd0fa9`) + this PR (3 Python files, no recompilation)\n- DSpark `{\"method\":\"dspark\",\"draft_sample_method\":\"greedy\",\"num_speculative_tokens\":5}`, `--max-num-batched-tokens 2048`, `--max-num-seqs 512`, fp8 KV, MARLIN mxfp4 MoE, V2 model runner\n\n**Before:** reproducible CUDA device-side assert in `map_draft_to_target` during draft warmup, ~35 s after weight load + graph capture — consistent with the 512 × 5 = 2560 rows over a 2048-row buffer described above. It was not a Marlin/mxfp4 issue.\n\n**After:** boot completes cleanly through the previously-fatal profiling/draft-warmup stage, **0 restarts**; DSpark CUDA graph capture 49/49, JIT warmup 102 keys. 🚀\n\n**Spec decode is functioning under real traffic:**\n- mean acceptance length **2.05–3.80**\n- per-position acceptance **0.85 / 0.70 / 0.55 / 0.41 / 0.27**\n- avg draft acceptance **21–56%**\n\nThanks again — happy to share logs or config if useful.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
