    "updated_at": "2026-09-16T13:00:30Z",
    "body": " Thanks @UmutAlihan  for testing the PR on the original H200 configuration and for sharing the detailed results. It’s great to hear that it now completes startup and is serving real traffic reliably. This also confirms that the original failure was caused by the profiling query-buffer overrun rather than the Marlin/mxfp4 backend.\r\n\r\nAgreed that dynamic K is a separate limitation from the static-K profiling fix in this PR. Since #51510 already tracks the missing V2 model-runner support, it would be better to continue that discussion there and keep this PR focused. The per-position acceptance numbers are useful evidence for that work.\r\n\r\nThanks again for taking the time to validate this!",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
